models/
# In a worktree this is a symlink to the main checkout's models/ so the 1.6GB
# whisper model and the 4.4GB refine model are not duplicated per branch. A
# symlink is a file to git, so `models/` alone does not cover it.
models
PatterDaemon.app/Contents/MacOS/
PatterDaemon.app/Contents/_CodeSignature/
# The whole bundle is generated by `patter build` from daemon/Info.plist.in. The
# identifier inside it is per-checkout, so committing it would hand one person's
# identity to every clone and put two bundles on one identifier the moment anyone
# ran a second checkout — the state that makes an Accessibility grant unfixable.
PatterDaemon.app/Contents/Info.plist
.bundle-id
# Your own whisper vocabulary, appended after the shared jargon.txt. Personal by
# definition: it is the words you say, which is not a thing to push to a shared repo.
jargon.local.txt
daemon.log
daemon.log.1
.DS_Store
servers.log
servers.log.1
.bench-tmp/
.probe-tmp/
.patter-rec.wav
# Retained microphone audio + pre-clean transcripts (`patter takes on`). Never
# commit these — they are raw recordings of whatever was said near the machine.
takes/
tcc-trace.log
# The design record and working notes. Kept LOCAL, not published: they interleave
# genuinely useful technical reasoning with verbatim transcripts of real
# conversations — including other people who never agreed to be published — and
# with client detail. CLAUDE.md is the public design record; these are the raw one.
# They are still the working files: edit and rely on them exactly as before.
*_LOG.md
*_TODO.md
